  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.2.6\n\n- Align the package version with the dependency maintenance release; contract behavior is unchanged.\n\n## 0.2.5\n\n- Reject serialized documents over the same 2 MiB UTF-8 ceiling enforced by Deserialize, with ContractDocumentInputLimitExceeded.\n\n## Service change on 2026-09-14\n\n- Echo moved the separate rule feed used by Mock.Client and Mock.Server to the paid plans. This was a service change, not a package release: an already installed 0.2.3 mock package can stop obtaining rules on Free without its package changing.\n- Contract generation and the contract APIs remain available on Free. Creating an application, managing its contract bindings and issuing a new key require the paid Applications surface; an existing active contract key can continue to use an existing binding.\n\n## 0.2.3\n\n- Render generated JSON with literal apostrophes, accented characters and HTML-sensitive characters for readable data responses.\n\n## 0.2.2\n\n- Add a producer client that publishes new versions of owned contracts and returns the server's compatibility verdict.\n- Keep publication independent of host frameworks and of the application's HTTP handler configuration.\n- Include NuGet release notes and symbols in the coordinated Echo package release.\n- Preserve contract generation behavior while aligning with the hosted authoring validation release.\n\n## 0.1.0\n\n- Provide the shared contract document codec, validation, inference and deterministic generation engine.",
